### 3. Example Custom Repo Script for PHP (`setup-php-repo.sh`)

Save this in your ADT repository (e.g., `${HOME}/providerscripts/webserver/setup-php-repo.sh`). It works cleanly across both **Ubuntu** (Ondřej PPA) and **Debian** (Sury) without requiring `software-properties-common` (`add-apt-repository`):

```sh
#!/bin/sh
set -eu

DISTRO=$(. /etc/os-release && printf '%s' "${ID}")
CODENAME=$(/usr/bin/lsb_release -cs)

/bin/mkdir -p /etc/apt/keyrings

case "${DISTRO}" in
    ubuntu)
        /usr/bin/gpg --batch --yes --dearmor \
            -o /etc/apt/keyrings/ondrej-php.gpg <<'EOF' || true
EOF
        # Fetch Ondrej Launchpad signing key directly
        /usr/bin/wget -qO- "https://keyserver.ubuntu.com/pks/lookup?op=get&search=0x14AA40EC0831756756D7F66C4F4EA0AAE5267A6C" \
            | /usr/bin/gpg --batch --yes --dearmor -o /etc/apt/keyrings/ondrej-php.gpg
        printf '%s\n' "deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/ondrej-php.gpg] https://ppa.launchpadcontent.net/ondrej/php/ubuntu ${CODENAME} main" \
            > /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ondrej-php.list
        ;;
    debian)
        /usr/bin/wget -qO /etc/apt/keyrings/sury-php.gpg https://packages.sury.org/php/apt.gpg
        printf '%s\n' "deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/sury-php.gpg] https://packages.sury.org/php/ ${CODENAME} main" \
            > /etc/apt/sources.list.d/sury-php.list
        ;;
    *)
        printf '%s\n' "ERROR: Unsupported distro for PHP repo setup: ${DISTRO}" >&2
        exit 1
        ;;
esac

